text:
isabel: Need a quick POC pack for NovaClinic — single WS multiplex, streaming with tool calls, strict JSON output, EU residency + SSO/KMS. Can we hand them code + legal blurb before EOD?

raj: Yes. Use session_id per logical stream. Hosted ok for demo; Dedicated w/ sticky routing recommended for ordered tool calls.

harry: Node snippet:

```js
// open, send schema_hints, handle tool_call
const WebSocket = require('ws');
const ws = new WebSocket(process.env.POC_WS);
ws.on('open', () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'open', session_id: 'sess1', schema_hints: { patient: { id: 'string' } } }));
});
ws.on('message', raw => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(raw);
  if (msg.type === 'tool_call') {
    // respond with JSON string
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'tool_response', session_id: msg.session_id, call_id: msg.call_id, result: JSON.stringify({ found: true }) }));
  }
});
```

raj: Handshake curl: 

curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/handshake -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"session_id":"sess1","schema_hints":{}}'
// returns {"ws_url":"wss://...","expires_in":900}

harry: Legal blurb: "Runtime keeps KV caches in-memory; no persistent storage of raw prompts/responses in Dedicated/Private unless logging enabled by customer. Customer-managed KMS supported. Audit logs available per contract."

isabel: Awesome. Also need a 1-week ballpark for 500 QPS on EU Dedicated.

raj: Rough: $20k-$40k for a short Dedicated test week depending on prompt sizes. Formal quote later.

deploy-bot: pool created: nova-poc-eu (p-nova-111)

isabel: Thanks — I'll send this to the customer.
